1. Interface Changes in JAVA 8:
--> Before Java 8, Interface should have only abstract methods(without body)
--> Java 8 allows the interfaces to have default and static methods.

Q) What is the advantage of having Default & Static methods in java 8? 
-> Default & Static methods provides backward compatibility. 
-> For example, if several classes such as A, B, C and D implements an interface Test then if we add a new method to the Test,
  we have to change the code in all the classes (A, B, C and D) that implements this interface.  

Ex: interface Test{
  }
class A implements Test{}
class B implements Test{}
class C implements Test{}
class D implements Test{}

In the above example we have only four classes that implements the interface, but imagine if there are hundreds of classes implementing an interface it will
become very difficult to change all the classes which are implementing that interface. That's why Java 8, we have a new concept "default methods"





